From a9a1f5e111d5bbceca9df3eafbfb93fa5179cc9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: whyrusleeping <why@ipfs.io>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 03:12:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] add a Config.ConnectionIDTracer to observe connection ID
 lifecycle events

Applications that demultiplex packets on a shared net.PacketConn need to know
which connection IDs belong to which connection. So far, the only way to learn
about connection IDs issued in NEW_CONNECTION_ID frames and retired via
RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames was a qlog Tracer, which requires constructing
qlog events for every packet sent and received.

The ConnectionIDTracer is notified when a connection ID is added to or
removed from the Transport's routing table for a connection. It is only
invoked on connection ID lifecycle events, and costs a nil check otherwise.
